From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Nov 2026 23:59:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1145 redfin: NFC persona: disable mode-set 6F 18 00
 (zero-length) for ANY persona NFCEE (eSE C0 and HCI network 01), not just C0

1144 made the eSE (NFCEE 0xC0) disable mode-set emit the zero-length completion
6F 18 00 so phNciNfc_CoreUtilsValRspLen accepts it. But the eSE teardown then
also disables the HCI network (NFCEE 0x01) with 22 01 02 01 00, which needs the
SAME 6F 18 00 completion; our 0x4000 path only sent it for id 0xC0. nfcd then
waits out the 9 s InitCompleteWdTimer and fails (DownloadRequest on main init;
DeInit/CORE_RESET on ReInit).

1145 generalizes the 0x4000 disable guard from "id == 0xC0" to "mode byte ==
0x00" for the NFCEE ids the persona manages (0xC0 OR 0x01): any such disable now
sends RSP 42 01 01 00 then 6F 18 00. The enable path (mode byte 01) is
unchanged: id 0xC0 still also gets 6F 20 02 C0 00, id 0x01 stays as before (no
6F 20). Still gated behind ese_pc_on() (fwif_fmt bit 0x4000); 0x8000 (alt
payload) and 0x10000 (deferral) stay present. Host-bound only via out_put;
nothing reaches the chip; gw_filter/tx_allowed untouched.

Caveat (confirm on-phone via a fresh oslog): 6F 18 00 passes the length
validator only if NFCEE 01's pending flag is set when it arrives;
phNciNfc_NfceeModeSetSequence should set it for the NFCEE being mode-set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC2fg7dvyvbEkjpmxxg
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_nfc.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_nfc.c
index 8d0a120..5d75eff 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_nfc.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_nfc.c
@@ -2088,8 +2088,11 @@ persona_packet(const uint8_t *p, unsigned n, uint8_t *out, unsigned *no, unsigne
 				}
 				return true;
 			}
-			if (ese_pc_on() && n > 4 && p[3] == 0xc0 && p[4] == 0x00) {
-				/* 1139/1144: disable: RSP, then 6F 18 00 (IceFall Power OFF, zero-length payload) completes the pending mode set; no 6F 20 */
+			if (ese_pc_on() && n > 4 && (p[3] == 0xc0 || p[3] == 0x01) && p[4] == 0x00) {
+				/* 1139/1144/1145: disable of any persona NFCEE (eSE C0 or HCI network 01): RSP, then 6F 18 00 (IceFall
+				 * Power OFF, zero-length payload) completes the pending mode set; no 6F 20. 1145 generalizes the
+				 * id==C0 guard to mode byte==0x00 so the eSE teardown's NFCEE 01 disable (22 01 02 01 00) gets the
+				 * same 6F 18 00 the length validator needs (NFCEE 01's pending flag is set by phNciNfc_NfceeModeSetSequence) */
 				static const uint8_t off1[3] = { 0x6f, 0x18, 0x00 };   /* 1144: zero-length payload; phNciNfc_CoreUtilsValRspLen needs the length byte 0 */
 				static const uint8_t off2[5] = { 0x6f, 0x18, 0x02, 0xc0, 0x00 };
 				bool alt = (nfc_fwif_fmt & 0x8000) != 0;
@@ -2099,7 +2102,7 @@ persona_packet(const uint8_t *p, unsigned n, uint8_t *out, unsigned *no, unsigne
 				out_put(out, no, cap, alt ? off2 : off1, alt ? sizeof(off2) : sizeof(off1));
 				persona_note(0x0201);
 				persona_step_say(p, n);
-				hci_log("host>", p, n, "NFCEE_MODE_SET C0 disable");
+				hci_log("host>", p, n, p[3] == 0x01 ? "NFCEE_MODE_SET 01 (HCI network) disable" : "NFCEE_MODE_SET C0 disable");
 				hci_log("<persona", r, len, "NFCEE_MODE_SET_RSP OK");
 				hci_log("<persona", alt ? off2 : off1, alt ? sizeof(off2) : sizeof(off1),
 				    alt ? "NXP 6F 18 (IceFall Power OFF) C0 status 00, fwif_fmt 0x8000 form (1139)" :
@@ -3086,7 +3089,7 @@ SYSCTL_UINT(_kern, OID_AUTO, sweet_nfc_fwif_fmt, CTLFLAG_RW | CTLFLAG_LOCKED, &n
     "0x80 = chip CRC state kept over Power 0; 1134: 0x100/0x200 = virtual eSE; 1136: 0x400 = + virtual HCI network, "
     "0x800 = 1137: also answer CORE_CONN_CREATE for the virtual NFCEE 01 (HCI conn 2); 1138: 0x1000 = eSE EoOP NTF "
     "6F 20 C0 after NFCEE_DISCOVER and MODE_SET C0, 0x2000 = GET_CONFIG A0EB returns the host-set value; 1139: 0x4000 = "
-    "MODE_SET C0 00 -> 6F 18 00 (1144; 0x8000: 6F 18 02 C0 00), no 6F 20, + A0EB mirror; 1140: 0x10000 = that NTF "
+    "MODE_SET C0/01 00 -> 6F 18 00 (1144; 1145: also for NFCEE 01; 0x8000: 6F 18 02 C0 00), no 6F 20, + A0EB mirror; 1140: 0x10000 = that NTF "
     "deferred by kern.sweet_nfc_ntf_delay_ms as its own packet, 0x20000 = no NTF after the disable RSP");
 
 static int
